  The Tsurugi is two-handed.  That means no shield.  (If you're not
wearing the highest enchanted shield you've found so far, why not?)
Cursed two-handed weapons are a deathtrap in Gehennom.  No praying
there.  No spell casting, no accessing containers of any kind wielding a
cursed two-handed weapon.

  #twoweaponing is superior to any twohanded weapon, because of silver
weapons and doubled damage bonus.  (There are no two-handed silver
weapons.)

  For singleweaponing two-handed weapons are losers due to loss of a
shield.  An elven shield gives base AC of +2 and can be safely enchanted
at +5.  That's up to 9 points of AC safely.  AC that works against every
monster when mobbed.  (And you *will* get mobbed.)

  Wielding Frost Brand gives cold resistance.  Wielding Fire Brand gives
fire resistance.  I've seen players keep them handy for use vs demons
with just those kinds of attacks.

  Excalibur gives the consistent damage and special effects.  Go with it
and then use a silver saber as your secondary weapon.

