  Strength.  Str:18/** does three more points of damage per hit than
Str:18/62.  When #twoweaponing that's an extra +6 damage.  If you don't
know about twoweaponing, look it up.  Be VERY CAREFUL when you start out
#twoweaponing.  It's got -9 to-hit and -3 damage at unskilled.  It also
uses the lesser of weapon skill and twoweapon skill.


>
>also also, i've been switching between +3 cloak of protection & +0
>cloak of displacement. which one would YOU choose? i'm thinking
>protection for the moment.
>
  Displacement means the monster wastes turns trying to hit where you're
not.  It's almost as good as using a ranged attack on a monster without
one.  Just remember to "re-activate" the cloak whenever the monster does
finally hit you.  Just move one square and the monster has to start
swinging blindly all over again.  

  Note: A cloak of displacement means a monster can guess your location
wrong by up to two squares.  Being invisible means a monster can guess
your location wrong by up to one square.  A properly used cloak of
displacement not only saves Hp, it's entertaining as well.






